WEBVTT

00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:07.866
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> This is Charlotte Campbell.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.849
She’s twenty-five and she’s a street performer, also known as a busker.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.445
Charlotte plays the guitar and sings on the South Bank in London.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:20.526
Today, she’s busking near the London Eye.

00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:24.020
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> On a typical day when I’m going busking,

00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:28.163
I get the train to Waterloo and I walk to the London Eye.

00:00:28.187 --> 00:00:31.707
I start at about eleven o’clock and I play until one.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.165
Then I take a lunch break.

00:00:33.293 --> 00:00:36.121
And sometimes I stay until six or seven p.m.,

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:39.756
but in the winter when it gets dark I go home a little earlier.

00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:44.586
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> You can find buskers everywhere – on the streets,

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:46.199
in shopping malls,

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:50.662
outside restaurants and in the parks of most big cities.

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:56.085
In some cities, you can also listen to music while you’re on the subway.

00:00:57.076 --> 00:01:04.431
Buskers play or sing all kinds of different music – opera, jazz, pop, and folk.

00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:10.533
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> I like music that’s on the radio, Ed Sheeran and things like that,

00:01:10.727 --> 00:01:14.187
and some older music from the 60s, like the Beatles.

00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:17.887
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> But busking isn’t always easy.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.197
Most big cities are busy and there are lots of buskers,

00:01:22.357 --> 00:01:26.005
which means you can’t just play music wherever you like.

00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:28.586
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> You need to get a permit to busk in London,

00:01:28.699 --> 00:01:30.996
and pass an audition, but when you do,

00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:34.338
there’s a really nice community and busking in London becomes easy.

00:01:35.709 --> 00:01:41.432
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> So buskers like Charlotte have to choose an area in the city to sing and play in.

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:49.585
They share this area with other buskers and sometimes they have to wait for the other buskers to finish.

00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:55.711
Charlotte lives in Brixton, in South London.

00:01:58.408 --> 00:02:02.674
In her apartment, she writes her own songs and practices.

00:02:11.376 --> 00:02:14.034
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> I love writing songs. I love writing my own music.

00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:19.470
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> For Charlotte, there are good and bad things about life as a busker.

00:02:19.494 --> 00:02:23.285
<v><b>Charlotte:</b></v> I like meeting new people and sharing my music with a new audience.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.633
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music on the streets of London

00:02:25.862 --> 00:02:27.669
I don’t like it when it gets cold.

00:02:27.782 --> 00:02:29.589
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music in my heart

00:02:30.106 --> 00:02:34.716
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music on the streets of London

00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:37.704
That’s where we are, that’s where we are

00:02:41.392 --> 00:02:44.911
Ah-hoo, yeah I get lonely

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:48.499
Ah-hoo, yeah I get cold

00:02:49.665 --> 00:02:54.113
Ah-hoo, I get tired, oh so tired

00:02:54.113 --> 00:02:57.145
But I’ll never sell my soul.

00:02:58.654 --> 00:03:02.160
Ah-hoo, from Piccadilly

00:03:03.386 --> 00:03:07.098
Ah-hoo, to Leicester Square

00:03:08.118 --> 00:03:11.448
Oh I gave my heart to London

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.560
And you’ll always find me there.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:22.077
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music on the streets of London

00:03:22.205 --> 00:03:25.753
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music in my heart

00:03:26.453 --> 00:03:31.226
Ba-baa, ba-baa, there’s music on the streets of London

00:03:31.993 --> 00:03:34.243
That’s where we are, that’s where we are